      "settlementKey": "aelvanyr:Sylvarielle",
      "description": "Mai Atomwake is a Drow ritual chemist who turns faith, chemistry, and survival horror into bottles people are desperate enough to drink. At the Sylvarielle Market Hall, she brews anti-fog tonics, ichor-laced protections, purification mixtures, and devotional compounds for the Choral Synod, always insisting that controlled contamination is better than ignorant exposure. She is sincere, unsettling, and scientifically useful, which is exactly why her work should never be left unsupervised.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Sylvarielle is a Village in Aelvanyr, under Participatory Democracy, with low danger, Farming, Partial forest, Deep forest terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin. Drow reads through the Half-Elf (choose an Elf Bloodline) entry of the race compendium, within Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, marked by Nebyrr. The local form is read through Half-Elf — Drow (Underdark). Half-elves are dual-natured beings born of human and elven lineage, often balancing ambition with longevity. They tend to struggle with identity but excel at diplomacy, adaptability, and bridging cultures. Table cues: +2 Charisma, +1 to Two Other Ability Scores, Darkvision, Fey Ancestry; starting tendency Neutral - Lawful - Cooperative - Neutral.",
      "rumors": [
